WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.550
The certificate samples
have a sharper problem.

2
00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:07.809
Learn's first example for adding a
certificate replaces every certificate the app

3
00:00:07.809 --> 00:00:12.687
had, so the old one vanishes the instant
the new one lands, with no overlap at all.

4
00:00:12.687 --> 00:00:16.901
The Key Vault example asks for six
months, which is just over the cap.

5
00:00:16.901 --> 00:00:21.133
And none of the samples ever puts
the renewed certificate on the app,

6
00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:23.400
asks the owner, or removes the old one.

7
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:27.883
So the verdict is: keep the version
one requests as models for the writes,

8
00:00:27.883 --> 00:00:30.220
and don't run any of them as published.
